## BE-X10-022 — CO2 multiplier: primary source FOUND

**Article 34, 1° of the Law of 25 November 2021** organising the fiscal and social greening of mobility (Belgian Official Gazette 3 December 2021, numac 2021033910), completing **Article 38, §3quater, 3° of the Law of 29 June 1981**, quoted verbatim: *"multipliée par un facteur de 2,25 à partir du 1er juillet 2023, par un facteur de 2,75 à partir du 1er janvier 2025, par un facteur de 4,00 à partir du 1er janvier 2026 et par un facteur de 5,50 à partir du 1er janvier 2027"* — corroborated by NSSO administrative instructions 2026/2 (special contributions, company vehicles), which reproduce the same four factors and dates. `CONFIRMED` and all four vendor names are gone.

The x4 figure was right; its sourcing was not. Two things the tier-B version got wrong or omitted, now in both artifacts: **the multiplier applies to the calculated contribution only, never to the minimum** (the law raises the minimum separately, to a non-indexed EUR 25.99 from 2026 — which independently matches the CCG's existing indexed EUR 42.34 and index 1.6291 = 185.85/114.08), and the "previously-stated 2.75" was not an error but the **2025** value. 5.50 from 2027, which the CCG had flagged as unverified, is confirmed by the same article.

**One thing the QA report got wrong, found by not trusting it.** §3 and §8 state the value and vendor names appear "in the CCG and nowhere else in the corpus." A corpus re-sweep found **WTC `Wage Type Catalogue!F59`** carrying `"4 for 2026 (CONFIRMED via Agoria/Cellule Mobilite/Van Mossel/Dynamik HR)"` — the same defect in the artifact that builds the levy as a wage type. Fixed with the same citation, plus a `Version Control` remark row. Post-fix sweep: zero vendor names in any live artifact; the four remaining occurrences are QA/review records of the finding itself. Re-verified as genuinely selector-only (order date, no value): DD `Country Fields!G167`, DmfA spec `Field Options!C36` and `Population Rules!D14`, SIR gap G22.

